 [17592186050598 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186092362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050598 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Inequalities Involving Geometric Sequences" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050598 #edb/ref 1033 1004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050598 #edb/ref 1034 1.1824841801908395 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050598 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5761edb2-80f5-563f-ad9c-bf729c12d152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1031 "The Product Rule for Exponents" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1033 267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050668 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5d74b293-aea3-563f-8c4c-f8febb13e3a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186078544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186078545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186078546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186078547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Geometric Sequences" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1033 679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050977 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "769cbed7-04cc-53d4-b34b-5d8b81d1dc47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078202 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078202 #edb/ref 1071 "The first term of a geometric sequence is $2$, and the common ratio is $3.$ What is the $9$th term?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078202 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6a49cd7-9558-524c-b511-b13bd792cfc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078202 #edb/ref 1074 "The first term is $a_1=2,$ and the common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}9}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =2\\cdot {3}^{9-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6561 \\\\  & =13\\,122\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is $a_{9}=13\\,122.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078203 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078203 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $9$, and the common ratio is $3,$ find the second term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078203 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7b26998-6137-54f9-bfe1-a2c3ba5eb0f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078203 #edb/ref 1074 "The common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $5$th term is $a_5=9,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{5-1} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot 81 \\\\ \\frac{9}{81} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=\\dfrac{1}{9},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second term is $a_2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078204 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1511" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078204 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the formula for the $n$th term of a sequence if the $6$th term is $80$ and the common ratio is $-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4bf89b8f-f713-51b5-8536-5aa5b08f16d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078204 #edb/ref 1074 "The common ratio is $r=-2,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $6$th term is $a_6=80,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{6-1} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-32) \\\\ -\\frac{80}{32} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=-\\dfrac{5}{2},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify a bit further by manipulating the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{-1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186549981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186550015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given the First Term and Common Ratio" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078558 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "01f44f8b-5db2-567a-89ce-9283f2f1b0c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186549940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186549942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Formula for the Nth Term of a Geometric Sequence" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078559 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5760a53a-1a0c-568e-ac9c-c820eaad3010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186549992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186549999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given a Term and the Common Ratio" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078560 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d82eb202-fec9-5769-a006-67d42b9323